# ============================================================================
# Private working files — never published
# ============================================================================
# This repo is public and publishes SOURCE CODE AND END-USER DOCS ONLY.
# Everything below stays on this machine and out of git history.
#
# Git ignore rules only control PUBLISHING. They have no effect on what you can
# read or write locally — keep using these files normally.

# Agent working state: specs, tickets, and source material for the local tracker.
.scratch/

# Agent-facing docs and project instructions.
# AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md and CONTEXT.md have no slash, so they match at ANY depth.
# That is deliberate: nested instruction files (packages/*/AGENTS.md) and
# per-context CONTEXT.md files stay covered, and over-matching only ever hides
# a file from git — it can never leak one. The one known collision is a future
# `docs/agents.md`, which would also be ignored; anchor with /AGENTS.md if that
# file ever needs to publish.
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
CONTEXT.md
docs/agents/
docs/adr/

# NOTE: `docs/` itself is deliberately NOT ignored, so future end-user docs
# (e.g. docs/usage.md) publish normally. Never ignore `docs/` wholesale.

# ============================================================================
# Dependencies and build output
# ============================================================================
node_modules/
dist/
